From c13992f0f415d81da40a54b1b5bf9fbe60d31ea2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Can Basaran <basaran.can@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:52:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] runner: league run guard (`league --guard FILE`, `admit
 --guard FILE`; Zeki #5385, review of cb669a0): served identity on every reply
 and a shared pre-send hard cap, kept by the runner

Identity (B2): a guard's expect_route names, per player, the model and provider every reply must carry
(exact match; the Gemini repeat: google/gemini-decision-1-20261111, Google AI Studio). DecisionClient::send
checks it after every successful response (warm-ups, decisions and each group of a split decision all go
through send), after the attempt's cost is booked; a missing or other model or provider sets the guard's
latch (in the process and in its latch file) and fails with a GuardStop. While the latch is set, a guarded
client sends nothing (checked before every attempt), `league` starts or resumes nothing (checked before the
database is opened) and `admit` refuses. A warm-up stops at once on a guard stop instead of retrying; a
match failing with a guard stop latches and cancels the league, which returns "stopped by its run guard"
(no deferral, no automatic re-entry). route_identity/identity_fields/ExpectRoute are ported from the
improve runner (1270c04/bbbea9d) into llm.rs, without its rejection log.

Money (B1): a guard's metered setups (by player name; their stored settings unchanged) get one shared
budget ledger and cap (budget.rs, as the Drex/Nace entries): every request attempt (warm-ups, retries,
failed attempts) reserves its worst case before it is sent and is refused (BudgetCap, typed; message
unchanged) when spent + reserved in flight + that would pass the cap; an answered attempt is settled at
max(list price, the provider's reported usage.cost) (decision clients now pass usage.cost), a refused or
unanswered one keeps its worst case. A refused reservation in a guarded league latches and stops it too.
A setup with a budget of its own is refused when the guard also meters it; a metered setup that is not a
decision service is refused. Without --guard nothing changes (Setup::guard None).

admit --guard: metered setups built with the guard's ledger read-only and immutable; the admitted-settings
record adds {"guard": {"path", "sha256"}}.

Tests (src/players/guard_tests.rs, offline: stub System One servers on 127.0.0.1, scratch ledgers, latch
files and databases): mismatched model, mismatched provider, missing provider/model, warm-up mismatch,
split-group mismatch (the later groups not sent), the latch surviving a restart (no request, no league
start, no database opened), a whole league stopping on a mismatch without re-entry; retries, warm-ups,
failed attempts (400, 200 without usage), two decisions in flight and an opponent's spend crossing the
shared cap (the entrant refused before sending). All 12 fail on cb669a0 (same tests, setup without the
guard) and pass here.
